#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:0
msgid ""
"Learn how to install snap on Fedora, enable classic snap support, test with "
"hello-world, and troubleshoot squashfs mount or Silverblue link issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:8
msgid "Install snap on Fedora"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:10
msgid "Snap can be installed on Fedora from the command line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:12
msgid "sudo dnf install snapd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:15
msgid ""
"Either log out and back in again, or restart your system, to ensure snap's "
"paths are updated correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:17
msgid ""
"To enable *classic* snap support, enter the following to create a symbolic "
"link between `/var/lib/snapd/snap` and `/snap`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:19
msgid "sudo ln -s /var/lib/snapd/snap /snap\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:23
msgid ""
"Either log out and back in again, or restart your system, to ensure snap’s "
"paths are updated correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:25
msgid ""
"To test your system, install the [hello-world](https://snapcraft.io/hello-"
"world) snap and make sure it runs correctly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:27
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap install hello-world\n"
"hello-world 6.3 from Canonical✓ installed\n"
"$ hello-world\n"
"Hello World!\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:33
msgid "Snap is now installed and ready to go."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:35
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:37
msgid ""
"system does not fully support snapd: cannot mount squashfs image using "
"\"squashfs\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:39
msgid ""
"Installing your first snap on a cloud image of Fedora may produce an error "
"similar to the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:41
msgid ""
"error: system does not fully support snapd: cannot mount squashfs image "
"using \"squashfs\": mount:\n"
"       /tmp/sanity-mountpoint-156693269: unknown filesystem type "
"'squashfs'.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:46
msgid ""
"If using a container, install the _fuse_ and _squashfuse_ packages (`sudo "
"dnf install fuse squashfuse`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:48
msgid ""
"Otherwise install _kernel-modules_ package (`sudo dnf install kernel-"
"modules`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:50
msgid "Fedora Silverblue prevents symbolic links"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/fedora.md:52
msgid ""
"[Fedora Silverblue](https://silverblue.fedoraproject.org/) implements a read-"
"only root filesystem and, consequently, cannot allow symbolic links to be "
"created. See the following associated GitHub issue for further details: "
"[Make it easier to link in or bind folders to the root directory?](https://"
"github.com/coreos/rpm-ostree/issues/1711)"
msgstr ""
